course: dictionary
lesson: 12823
title: Emigrant: leaving home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An emigrant is a person who leaves their own country to live in another country. The word comes from «emigrate», which means to leave your home country and settle somewhere else. When you read it, look for clues: the sentence will often tell you what country someone left and where they went.
explain: Do not mix it up with immigrant. An emigrant leaves a country, but an immigrant arrives in one. The two words describe the same move, seen from two different places. Ask yourself: is the person leaving, or arriving? That question will help you choose the right word.
explain: People become emigrants for many reasons, such as poverty, war, or looking for new chances in work. «Many Irish emigrants sailed to America in the 1840s.» The clues are Irish, which tells you where they came from, and sailed to America, which tells you where they went. So an emigrant is someone who moves from one country to live in another.
fact: An emigrant is a person who leaves their own country to live in another country.
fact: «Emigrant» comes from «emigrate», which means to leave your country and settle in another one.
fact: Emigrants often leave because of poverty, war, or to find new chances.
fact: «Irish emigrants» moved abroad during the Great Famine of the 1840s.
fact: An emigrant leaves a country, while an immigrant arrives in a country. Both words describe the same kind of move.
exercise: «Many Irish emigrants sailed to America.» Which country did the emigrants leave? | The sea | America | Scotland | *Ireland
exercise: What is an emigrant? | A person who visits a country for one week on holiday | A person who builds boats for a living | *A person who leaves their own country to live in another country
exercise: «The Lopez family became emigrants when they moved to Canada for work.» Which word means a person who arrives in a country to live there? | Visitor | Builder | Emigrant | *Immigrant
test: Why might a family become emigrants? | To watch a football match in a stadium abroad | To buy a new car in a shop | *To escape war or poverty and look for new chances
test: «Tomas left Poland and made his home in Canada.» What is Tomas? | An ancient king | A builder of castles | A visitor on a short holiday | *An emigrant from Poland
exam: Which phrase is closest in meaning to emigrant? | *A person who leaves home to live abroad | A person who grows food on a farm | A person who is very old | A person who sings in a choir
